title: Resolve a major reform vote

@resolve
title: Verify authority to carry the bill
go-to: authority_lost if left_in_government = 0 or government_has_confidence = 0 or caretaker_government = 1; count if left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0

@authority_lost
title: The mandate disappears before the count
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const issue = Q.reform_pressure_issue;
if (issue) {
    Q[issue + "_reform_proposal_stage"] =
        Number(Q[issue + "_reform_goal_stage"]) || 4;
}
Q.reform_pressure_pending = 0;
Q.reform_pressure_mode = "None";
Q.reform_pressure_cooldown = 2;
Q.reform_pressure_due_time = -1;
Q.reform_pressure_rounds = 0;
Q.reform_pressure_return_mode = "card";
Q.reform_pressure_last_result =
    "The bill is deferred because Lewica no longer has governing authority";
Q.news_headline = Q.reform_pressure_last_result;
!}

The cabinet lost confidence, entered caretaker status or lost Lewica before
the delayed confrontation could be resolved. No law is enacted and no project
momentum is confiscated; the ambitious bill returns when governing authority
does.

- @poland_polling: Carry the deferred bill into the next month

@count
title: Count the coalition and the Palace
on-arrival: {!
// One shared model decides what is reachable. Every negotiating action in
// poland_reform_pressure moves an input of that model, which is the whole
// point: the old code capped tiers from the president's name before it read a
// single commitment, so bargaining could never change the answer.
Q.reform_ceiling_issue = Q.reform_pressure_issue;
Q.reform_ceiling_target = Math.max(
    1,
    Math.min(4, Math.round(Number(Q.reform_pressure_target_stage) || 1))
);
if (Q.reform_pressure_return_mode != "pressure") {
    Q.reform_pressure_forced = 0;
    Q.reform_pressure_rounds = 0;
}
!}
call: poland_reform_ceiling
go-to: verdict

@verdict
title: The bill meets its veto players
on-arrival: {!
const issue = Q.reform_pressure_issue;
const target = Number(Q.reform_ceiling_target_resolved) || 1;
const forcedTier = Q.reform_pressure_forced ? 1 : 0;
// Forcing the issue buys exactly one tier above what the coalition would
// otherwise tolerate, and puts the government at risk for it.
const effectiveCeiling =
    Number(Q.reform_ceiling_tier) + (forcedTier ? 1 : 0);
const blocked = target > effectiveCeiling ? 1 : 0;
Q.reform_pressure_issue_name = Q[issue + "_reform_display_name"] || issue;

if (blocked) {
    Q[issue + "_reform_proposal_stage"] = target;
    Q.reform_pressure_pending = 1;
    Q.reform_pressure_mode = "partner_objection";
    Q.reform_pressure_actor = Q.reform_ceiling_blocker;
    Q.reform_pressure_actor_name = Q.reform_ceiling_blocker_name;
    Q.reform_pressure_intensity = Math.min(
        100,
        28 + target * 10 + Number(Q.reform_ceiling_gap) * 0.3 +
        (Q.reform_ceiling_blocker == "president" ? 8 : 0) +
        (Q.hard_mode ? 8 : 0)
    );
    Q.reform_pressure_illegality = 0;
    Q.reform_pressure_due_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
    Q.reform_pressure_objections += 1;
    Q.news_headline = Q.reform_ceiling_blocker_name +
        " blocks Lewica's " + Q.reform_pressure_issue_name +
        " at tier " + target;
} else {
    const forced = forcedTier;
    Q[issue + "_reform_stage"] = target;
    Q[issue + "_reform_proposal_stage"] = target;
    Q[issue + "_reform_defined"] = 1;
    Q[issue + "_reform_settled"] = 1;
    Q[issue + "_on_slate"] = 1;
    Q[issue + "_reform_progress"] = Math.max(
        Number(Q[issue + "_reform_progress"]) || 0,
        target * 20
    );
    // Tier 1 is a defeat dressed as a law: it scores negative on purpose.
    const deliveryByStage = [0, -2, 2, 4, 8];
    const trustByStage = [0, -2, 1, 2, 5];
    const credibilityByStage = [0, -4, 4, 8, 16];
    const audienceByStage = [0, -3, 3, 6, 12];
    const pollByStage = [0, -0.8, 0.6, 1.2, 3.0];
    const forcedPollBonus = [0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.9, 1.5];
    const rivalPenaltyByStage = [0, -0.15, 0.10, 0.25, 0.55];
    const forcedRivalPenalty = [0, 0.05, 0.10, 0.15, 0.20];
    const opinionByStage = [0, -3, 2, 4, 7];
    const forcedOpinionBonus = [0, 0, 1, 2, 4];
    const ownershipByStage = [0, -4, 2, 5, 9];
    const blocBoostByStage = [0, 0, 0.5, 1, 2];
    const forcedBlocBonus = [0, 0, 0, 0.5, 1];
    const voterBlocs = [
        "metropolitan_liberals", "liberal_professionals",
        "public_service_families", "industrial_logistics",
        "provincial_welfare", "rural_localists",
        "older_welfare_households", "anti_establishment_youth"
    ];
    // Every reform belongs to a public-mood field and to a family. Enacting one
    // moves its own field hard and its neighbours a little: that spillover is
    // the progressive wave, or the backlash, becoming visible.
    const issueFields = {
        abortion: { field: "abortion_rights", family: "rights" },
        marriage: { field: "lgbt_equality", family: "rights" },
        church: { field: "secular_state", family: "rights" },
        asylum: { field: "refugee_solidarity", family: "borders" },
        border: { field: "border_security", family: "borders" },
        defence: { field: "national_security", family: "borders" },
        labor: { field: "social_spending", family: "material" },
        health: { field: "vaccination", family: "material" },
        courts: { field: "rule_of_law", family: "institutions" }
    };
    const issueEffects = {
        abortion: {
            credibility: "feminist_trust",
            audience: "progressive_credibility",
            goal: "government_goal_equality"
        },
        marriage: {
            credibility: "progressive_credibility",
            audience: "minority_safety",
            goal: "government_goal_equality"
        },
        church: {
            credibility: "progressive_credibility",
            audience: "urban_progressive_support",
            goal: "government_goal_equality"
        },
        asylum: {
            credibility: "progressive_credibility",
            audience: "minority_safety",
            goal: "government_goal_equality"
        },
        border: {
            credibility: "government_delivery",
            audience: "public_trust",
            goal: ""
        },
        defence: {
            credibility: "government_delivery",
            audience: "public_trust",
            goal: ""
        },
        labor: {
            credibility: "labor_credibility",
            audience: "workers_support",
            goal: "government_goal_labor"
        },
        health: {
            credibility: "labor_credibility",
            audience: "public_sector_support",
            goal: "government_goal_labor"
        },
        courts: {
            credibility: "judicial_legitimacy",
            audience: "public_trust",
            goal: ""
        }
    };
    const clampOpinion = function(key, change) {
        Q[key] = Math.max(
            0,
            Math.min(100, (Number(Q[key]) || 0) + change)
        );
    };
    const pollSwing = pollByStage[target] +
        (forced ? forcedPollBonus[target] : 0);
    const rivalPenalty = rivalPenaltyByStage[target] +
        (forced ? forcedRivalPenalty[target] : 0);
    const opinionShift = opinionByStage[target] +
        (forced ? forcedOpinionBonus[target] : 0);
    const broadBlocBoost = blocBoostByStage[target] +
        (forced ? forcedBlocBonus[target] : 0);
    const field = issueFields[issue].family;
    const opinionKey = issueFields[issue].field;
    const effects = issueEffects[issue];
    Q.government_delivery += deliveryByStage[target];
    Q.public_trust += trustByStage[target] +
        (forced && target >= 3 ? target - 2 : 0);
    Q.left_poll += pollSwing;
    for (const rival of ["pis", "ko", "psl", "p2050", "konf"]) {
        Q[rival + "_poll"] = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q[rival + "_poll"]) || 0) - rivalPenalty
        );
    }
    for (const bloc of voterBlocs) {
        const affinityKey = bloc + "_left_affinity";
        Q[affinityKey] = (Number(Q[affinityKey]) || 0) + broadBlocBoost;
    }
    clampOpinion(opinionKey + "_support", opinionShift);
    clampOpinion(opinionKey + "_backlash", -opinionShift);
    clampOpinion(
        opinionKey + "_left_ownership",
        ownershipByStage[target] + (forced ? target + 1 : 0)
    );
    clampOpinion(
        opinionKey + "_salience",
        (target == 1 ? 2 : target) + (forced ? target : 0)
    );
    // Spillover across the family: a delivered settlement makes the adjacent
    // arguments easier, and a humiliating tier-1 climbdown makes them harder.
    if (target != 1) {
        for (const other of Object.keys(issueFields)) {
            if (other == issue || issueFields[other].family != field) {
                continue;
            }
            clampOpinion(
                issueFields[other].field + "_support",
                opinionShift * 0.35
            );
            clampOpinion(
                issueFields[other].field + "_left_ownership",
                ownershipByStage[target] * 0.30
            );
        }
    }
    Q[effects.credibility] =
        (Number(Q[effects.credibility]) || 0) + credibilityByStage[target];
    Q[effects.audience] =
        (Number(Q[effects.audience]) || 0) + audienceByStage[target];
    if (effects.goal) {
        Q[effects.goal] = 1;
    }
    if (issue == "abortion" && target >= 1) {
        Q.abortion_law_enacted = 1;
    }
    if (issue == "courts") {
        Q.legal_dualism = Math.max(
            0, (Number(Q.legal_dualism) || 0) - target * 3
        );
        Q.judicial_repair_mandate =
            (Number(Q.judicial_repair_mandate) || 0) + target * 2;
    }
    if (issue == "church") {
        Q.anticlerical_edge = Math.max(
            0, Math.min(100, (Number(Q.anticlerical_edge) || 0) + target * 3)
        );
    }
    const settlementLabel = Q[issue + "_reform_label_" + target];
    Q.last_policy_stage = "Enacted settlement: " + settlementLabel;
    Q.last_policy_authority = Q.reform_pressure_palace_override
        ? "Three-fifths Sejm veto override"
        : forced
            ? "Lewica-forced coalition vote and President " + Q.president_name
            : "Sejm majority and President " + Q.president_name;
    Q.last_policy_implementation = 1;
    Q.news_headline = Q.reform_pressure_issue_name +
        (forced ? " survives coalition opposition with " : " closes with ") +
        settlementLabel.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + settlementLabel.slice(1);
    // Feed the existing public-mood reception panel so the ledger shows the
    // reform as the latest public test rather than staying silent about it.
    Q.public_opinion_last_issue = opinionKey;
    Q.public_opinion_last_action =
        "Enacted " + Q.reform_pressure_issue_name;
    Q.public_opinion_last_delta = Math.round(opinionShift);
    Q.public_opinion_last_reception = target >= 3
        ? "breakthrough"
        : (target == 2 ? "favourable" : "backlash");
    Q.reform_pressure_forced = 0;
    Q.reform_pressure_rounds = 0;
}
!}
go-to: poland_reform_pressure if reform_pressure_return_mode = "pressure" and reform_pressure_pending = 1; pressure_enacted if reform_pressure_return_mode = "pressure" and reform_pressure_pending = 0; objection_queued if reform_pressure_return_mode != "pressure" and reform_pressure_pending = 1; enacted if reform_pressure_return_mode != "pressure" and reform_pressure_pending = 0

@enacted
title: The reform enters the statute book
new-page: true

**[+ news_headline +].** This is the final settlement of this project. A
compromise law is not the first rung of a later automatic climb; accepting and
enacting it closes the chapter at that outcome.

[? if reform_ceiling_tier > reform_ceiling_target_resolved: The coalition would
have carried more than we asked for. That headroom is now spent.?]

- #poland_card_finish

@objection_queued
title: A veto player withholds the bill
new-page: true

**[+ reform_ceiling_blocker_name +] blocks the bill at tier [+
reform_ceiling_target_resolved +].** The settlement ceiling this month is **[+
reform_ceiling_tier_label +]**.

[+ reform_ceiling_blocker_name +] scores the bill at **[+
reform_ceiling_blocker_score +]** against the **[+ reform_ceiling_need +]** a
tier-[+ reform_ceiling_target_resolved +] settlement needs.

The confrontation arrives when the month closes. Lewica may buy commitments,
cash in a relationship, settle on the reachable tier, or force the issue and
put the coalition under threat.

- #poland_card_finish

@pressure_enacted
title: The coalition and Palace count closes
new-page: true
on-arrival: reform_pressure_last_result = news_headline; reform_pressure_return_mode = "card"; reform_pressure_palace_override = 0

The remaining veto players have been counted in sequence. **[+
news_headline +].** The enacted settlement closes this project, whether it
preserved the original ambitious bill or survived only after being forced
down.

- @poland_polling: Carry the enacted settlement into the new month
